# §63. Taxable income defined

> Module Section63

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraIncome as Inc
> Using SaraStatus as St
> Using SaraPredicates as P
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using Section7703 as S7703
> Using Section152 as S152
> Using Section151 as S151
> Using Section68 as S68

Port of `section63.pl`. §63 defines taxable income as gross income less
deductions, and defines the standard deduction that an individual who does not
itemize takes instead.

§63 sits on the §151 → §68 → §63 → §151 cycle. The cycle is cut at §68(b) —
the applicable amount is a pure function of filing status, so §151(d)(3) can
reach it without coming back through §63 — which lets §63 depend on §151 and
§68 outright. See `Section151.catala_en` for the argument. Subsection query
scopes that predate the cut still take the two figures as inputs, since the
cases supply them by injection.

## (c)(7) Special rules for 2018 through 2025

Substitutes $18,000 for the head-of-household figure in (c)(2)(B) and $12,000
for the residual figure in (c)(2)(C).

```catala-metadata
declaration in_2018_2025 content boolean
  depends on y content integer
  equals y > 2017 and y < 2026

declaration head_of_household_basic content money
  depends on y content integer
  equals if in_2018_2025 of y then $18,000 else $4,400

declaration residual_basic content money
  depends on y content integer
  equals if in_2018_2025 of y then $12,000 else $3,000
```

## (c)(2) Basic standard deduction

(A) doubles the residual figure for a joint return or a surviving spouse; (B)
gives heads of household their own figure; (C) is everyone else.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope BasicStandardDeduction:
  input status content St.Status
  input taxable_year content integer
  output doubled content boolean
  output amount content money
```

```catala
scope BasicStandardDeduction:
  definition doubled equals status = St.Status.JointOrSurvivingSpouse

  definition amount equals residual_basic of taxable_year
  exception definition amount
    under condition status = St.Status.HeadOfHousehold
    consequence equals head_of_household_basic of taxable_year
  exception definition amount
    under condition doubled
    consequence equals (residual_basic of taxable_year) * (decimal of 2)
```

## (f) Aged or blind additional amounts

§63(f) counts the taxpayer's entitlements — aged self, aged spouse, blind self,
blind spouse — and multiplies by $600, or $750 for an individual who is neither
married nor a surviving spouse.

The age test is written in the Prolog as a comparison of two *durations* rather
than of two dates: the span from birth to the last day of the taxable year
against the span from that day to the last day of the year 65 years later.
Because those two windows contain different numbers of leap days the test is
not exactly "age >= 65", so the port compares the same two spans rather than
substituting a date comparison.

**The blind-spouse count is 600, not 1** — see `sara_scripts/DEVIATIONS.md` D6.
That is a defect in the gold, reproduced here deliberately.

```catala-metadata
declaration attained_65 content boolean
  depends on birth content date, y content integer
  equals
    ((W.last_day_year of y) - birth)
      >= ((W.last_day_year of (y + 65)) - (W.last_day_year of y))

declaration per_entitlement content money
  depends on married content boolean, surviving_spouse content boolean
  equals if (not married) and (not surviving_spouse) then $750 else $600

declaration scope AgedOrBlind:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input surviving_spouse content boolean
  ## The §7703 spouses for whom §151(b) allows the additional exemption --- a
  ## *list*, because `s63_f_1_B(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy)` carries one `Spouse` through
  ## both halves of the clause: the same person has to be over 65 *and* be the
  ## one §151(b) allows. Reading the two halves off different spouses gave a
  ## couple filing jointly a $600 entitlement SARA never grants; see D80. The
  ## cases inject this, and D2 records that the Prolog's arity-2 guard is
  ## vacuous.
  input exempt_spouses content list of W.Entity
  output aged_self content boolean
  output aged_spouse content boolean
  output blind_self content boolean
  output blind_spouse content boolean
  output counts content integer
  output additional content money
```

```catala
scope AgedOrBlind:
  # A grant answers the goal; a grant made *without* `discontiguous` also
  # removes the birth-date derivation, and then only a matching row can. Here
  # failing is an ordinary outcome rather than an unavailable value -- the
  # Prolog wraps it in `( ... -> Count1 is 1 ; Count1 is 0 )` -- so this needs
  # `pred_available` and no `applies` companion. See D57.
  definition aged_self equals
    (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_A_2,
       [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    or
    ((not (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_A_2))
     and (exists ev among world.events such that
            ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Birth
            and ev.agents contains taxpayer
            and (exists d among ev.starts such that attained_65 of d, taxable_year)))

  definition aged_spouse equals
    (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_B_3,
       [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    or
    ((not (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_B_3))
    and married
    and (exists sp among exempt_spouses such that
           exists ev among world.events such that
             ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Birth
             and ev.agents contains sp
             and (exists d among ev.starts
                  such that attained_65 of d, taxable_year)))

  definition blind_self equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Blindness
      and ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and (exists d among ev.starts
           such that d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))

  definition blind_spouse equals
    married
    and (exists sp among exempt_spouses such that
           exists ev among world.events such that
             ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Blindness
             and ev.agents contains sp
             and (exists d among ev.starts
                  such that d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))

  definition counts equals
    (if aged_self then 1 else 0)
    + (if aged_spouse then 1 else 0)
    + (if blind_self then 1 else 0)
    # DEVIATIONS.md D6: the gold uses 600 here where every sibling uses 1.
    + (if blind_spouse then 600 else 0)

  definition additional equals
    (per_entitlement of married, surviving_spouse) * (decimal of counts)
```

## (d) Itemized deductions

Collected from `deduction_` events the taxpayer is the agent of, whose start
date falls inside the taxable year. The Prolog requires at least one such
deduction (`length(Amounts,L), L>0`), so a taxpayer with none does not itemize
at all — which is what routes them to §63(b).

As in `SaraIncome`, `amount_/2` and `start_/2` are relations, so the sum is over
the cross product of amounts and in-window start dates.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ItemizedDeductions:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output itemizes content boolean
  output total content money
```

```catala
scope ItemizedDeductions:
  definition total equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events
         such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Deduction
                   and e.agents contains taxpayer)
       to (Inc.event_contribution of ev, taxable_year)
          # `agent_/2` is a relation like the other two: stating it twice gives
          # the `findall` two solutions and counts the deduction twice. Same
          # reading as D40, one section over. See D56.
          * (decimal of (Inc.role_count of ev.agents, taxpayer)))

  # `length(Amounts,L), L>0` counts the `findall`'s solutions, and every goal
  # in it has to succeed for there to be one -- `amount_(Deduction,Amount)`
  # included. A deduction event with a date but no amount is not a solution, so
  # the taxpayer does not itemize and §63(b) takes over. See D72.
  definition itemizes equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Deduction
      and ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and (number of ev.amounts) > 0
      and (exists d among ev.starts such that
             (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= d
             and d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
```

## (c)(6) Individuals not eligible for the standard deduction

(A) a married individual filing separately where either spouse itemizes, (B) a
nonresident alien, (D) an estate, trust, common trust fund or partnership. For
(B) and (D) the Prolog treats a missing start or end date as "no constraint",
which is the `var`/`nonvar` idiom and becomes an empty list here.

```catala-metadata
declaration overlaps_year content boolean
  depends on ev content W.Event, y content integer
  equals
    ((number of ev.starts) = 0
     or (exists d among ev.starts such that d <= (W.last_day_year of y)))
    and ((number of ev.ends) = 0
         or (exists d among ev.ends such that (W.first_day_year of y) <= d))

declaration scope NotEligible:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input joint_return content boolean
  ## Every §7703 spouse, not the first: the Prolog backtracks over
  ## `s7703(Taxp,Spouse,_,Taxy)` and any of them may be the one who itemizes.
  ## See D71.
  input spouses content list of W.Entity
  output subparagraph_a content boolean
  output subparagraph_b content boolean
  output subparagraph_d content boolean
  output not_eligible content boolean
```

```catala
scope NotEligible:
  definition subparagraph_a equals
    married and not joint_return
    and (exists ev among world.events such that
           ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Deduction
           and (ev.agents contains taxpayer
                or (exists sp among spouses such that ev.agents contains sp))
           and (exists d among ev.starts such that
                  (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= d
                  and d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))

  definition subparagraph_b equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.NonresidentAlien
      and ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and overlaps_year of ev, taxable_year

  definition subparagraph_d equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.BusinessTrust
      and ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and overlaps_year of ev, taxable_year

  definition not_eligible equals
    subparagraph_a or subparagraph_b or subparagraph_d
```

## (c)(5) Limitation for certain dependents

Where a §151 deduction is allowable to another taxpayer for this individual, the
basic standard deduction is capped at the greater of $500 and $250 plus the
individual's earned income. The Prolog reads "earned income" as gross income.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope DependentCap:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §151(b)/(c) allowable to another taxpayer, derived by §151 now that the
  ## section exists; the cases also inject it directly.
  input dependent_of_another content boolean
  output capped content boolean
  output cap content money
```

```catala
scope DependentCap:
  definition capped equals
    dependent_of_another
    or (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s151_b_applies_3,
          [-1; taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    or (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s151_c_applies_3,
          [-1; taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])

  definition cap equals
    Money.max of $500,
      ($250 + (output of Inc.GrossIncomeIndividual with {
                 -- world: world -- person: taxpayer
                 -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).total)
```

## Query surfaces used by the cases

```catala-metadata
## s63_c_7_i(Taxy,Amount) and s63_c_7_ii(Taxy,Amount)
declaration scope SpecialRuleHolds:
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## true for clause (i) -- the head-of-household substitution
  input is_clause_i content boolean
  input claimed content money
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_2_C(Taxy,Bassd)
declaration scope ResidualBasicHolds:
  input taxable_year content integer
  input claimed content money
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_2_B(Taxp,Taxy,Bassd)
declaration scope HeadOfHouseholdBasicHolds:
  input status content St.Status
  input taxable_year content integer
  input claimed content money
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope SpecialRuleHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (in_2018_2025 of taxable_year)
    and claimed = (if is_clause_i then $18,000 else $12,000)

scope ResidualBasicHolds:
  definition holds equals (residual_basic of taxable_year) = claimed

scope HeadOfHouseholdBasicHolds:
  definition holds equals
    status = St.Status.HeadOfHousehold
    and (head_of_household_basic of taxable_year) = claimed
```

## Remaining query surfaces

These expose the subsections above in the shape the cases query them, so that
every scope in this module is reachable from the suite rather than merely
typechecking. Argument orders follow the Prolog exactly, which is not uniform:
`s63_c_3(Taxp,Addsd,Taxy)` puts the amount second while
`s63_f_3(Taxp,Taxy,Amount)` puts it third.

```catala-metadata
## s63_f_1_A(Taxp,Taxy), s63_f_1_B(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy),
## s63_f_2_A(Taxp,Taxy), s63_f_2_B(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy)
declaration enumeration AgedBlindClause:
  -- AgedSelf
  -- AgedSpouse
  -- BlindSelf
  -- BlindSpouse

declaration scope AgedBlindClauseHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input surviving_spouse content boolean
  input exempt_spouses content list of W.Entity
  input clause content AgedBlindClause
  output holds content boolean

## s63_f_3(Taxp,Taxy,Amount) -- the $750 substitution
declaration scope HigherAmountHolds:
  input married content boolean
  input surviving_spouse content boolean
  input claimed content money
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_3(Taxp,Addsd,Taxy) -- the additional standard deduction
declaration scope AdditionalDeductionHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input surviving_spouse content boolean
  input exempt_spouses content list of W.Entity
  input claimed content money
  output holds content boolean

## s63_d(Taxp,Itemded,Total_amount,Taxy)
declaration scope ItemizedTotalHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input claimed content optional of money
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_6_A/4, s63_c_6_B/2, s63_c_6_D/2
declaration enumeration IneligibleClause:
  -- ClauseA
  -- ClauseB
  -- ClauseD

declaration scope NotEligibleClauseHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input joint_return content boolean
  input spouses content list of W.Entity
  input clause content IneligibleClause
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_5(Taxp,S45,Grossinc,Taxy,Bassd)
declaration scope DependentCapHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input claimed content optional of money
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output dependent_of_another content boolean
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_2_A_i(Taxp,Joint_return,Taxy) and s63_c_2_A_ii(Taxp,Taxy)
declaration scope DoubledBasicHolds:
  input married content boolean
  input joint_return content boolean
  input surviving_spouse content boolean
  ## true for clause (i) -- the joint-return route
  input is_clause_i content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope AgedBlindClauseHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (let ab equals
       (output of AgedOrBlind with {
          -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- taxable_year: taxable_year
          -- married: married -- surviving_spouse: surviving_spouse
          -- exempt_spouses: exempt_spouses }) in
     match clause with pattern
     -- AgedSelf: ab.aged_self
     -- AgedSpouse: ab.aged_spouse
     -- BlindSelf: ab.blind_self
     -- BlindSpouse: ab.blind_spouse)

scope HigherAmountHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (not married) and (not surviving_spouse)
    and (per_entitlement of married, surviving_spouse) = claimed

scope AdditionalDeductionHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (output of AgedOrBlind with {
       -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- married: married -- surviving_spouse: surviving_spouse
       -- exempt_spouses: exempt_spouses }).additional
      = claimed

scope ItemizedTotalHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (let d equals
       (output of ItemizedDeductions with {
          -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- taxable_year: taxable_year }) in
     d.itemizes
     and (match claimed with pattern
          -- Absent: true
          -- Present content c: d.total = c))

scope NotEligibleClauseHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (let n equals
       (output of NotEligible with {
          -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- taxable_year: taxable_year -- married: married
          -- joint_return: joint_return -- spouses: spouses }) in
     match clause with pattern
     -- ClauseA: n.subparagraph_a
     -- ClauseB: n.subparagraph_b
     -- ClauseD: n.subparagraph_d)

scope DependentCapHolds:
  ## §151(b)/(c) allowable to *another* taxpayer for this individual, which is
  ## exactly the disallowance test §151(d)(2) runs.
  definition dependent_of_another equals
    (output of S151.Individual with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world
       -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).disallowed

  definition holds equals
    (let d equals
       (output of DependentCap with {
          -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- taxable_year: taxable_year
          -- dependent_of_another: dependent_of_another }) in
     d.capped
     and (match claimed with pattern
          -- Absent: true
          -- Present content c: d.cap = c))

scope DoubledBasicHolds:
  definition holds equals
    if is_clause_i then (married and joint_return) else surviving_spouse
```

## (c) and (c)(1) — the standard deduction as a value

`s63_c/3` is `s63_c_1/3`, which is zero for an individual (c)(6) makes
ineligible and otherwise the basic amount from (c)(1)(A) plus the additional
amount from (c)(1)(B). (c)(1)(A) caps the basic amount by (c)(5) where that
paragraph bites.

Each level a case can grant is an exception here: `s63_c/3`, `s63_c_1/3`,
`s63_c_2/3` and `s63_c_3/3` are all injected somewhere in the corpus.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope StandardDeduction:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output status content St.Status
  ## (c)(6)
  output not_eligible content boolean
  ## (c)(2), before the (c)(5) cap
  output basic_uncapped content money
  ## (c)(1)(A)
  output basic content money
  ## The §7703 spouses §151(b) allows an additional exemption for
  output exempt_spouses content list of W.Entity
  ## (c)(1)(B) = s63_c_3 = §63(f)
  output additional content money
  ## s63_c_1/3 and s63_c/3
  output amount content money
```

```catala
scope StandardDeduction:
  definition status equals
    (output of St.FilingStatus with {
       -- world: world -- injections: injections
       -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).status

  definition not_eligible equals
    (output of NotEligible with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- married: (output of St.FilingStatus with {
                      -- world: world -- injections: injections
                      -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                      -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).married
       -- joint_return: (output of St.FilingStatus with {
                           -- world: world -- injections: injections
                           -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                           -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).joint_return
       -- spouses: (output of S7703.MaritalStatusA with {
                      -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                      -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).spouses }).not_eligible

  definition basic_uncapped equals
    (output of BasicStandardDeduction with {
       -- status: status -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).amount

  exception definition basic_uncapped
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_c_2_3,
         [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
    consequence equals
      (match (W.injected_money of injections, P.pred_s63_c_2_3,
                [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1], 3) with pattern
       -- Absent: $0
       -- Present content m: m)

  definition basic equals
    (let d equals
       (output of DependentCap with {
          -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- taxable_year: taxable_year
          -- dependent_of_another:
               (output of S151.Individual with {
                  -- injections: injections -- world: world
                  -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                  -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                  -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                  -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                  -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
                  -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
                  -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
                  -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).disallowed }) in
     if d.capped then Money.min of basic_uncapped, d.cap else basic_uncapped)

  # Every spouse for whom `s151_b_applies(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy)` holds: §151
  # derives the set, and a grant contributes the spouse it names --- or, where
  # it left that argument free, every spouse §7703 offers, because the free
  # variable unifies with each in turn. Replacing the predicate leaves nothing
  # but the rows. See D22 and D80.
  definition exempt_spouses equals
    (let indiv equals
       (output of S151.Individual with {
          -- injections: injections -- world: world
          -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year
          -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
          -- descendent_of: descendent_of
          -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
          -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
          -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
          -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
          -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }) in
     (let granted equals
        (combine all r
           among (map each inj among
                   (W.injections_for of injections, P.pred_s151_b_applies_3,
                      [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
                  to (match (W.injection_entity of inj, 2) with pattern
                      -- Absent: indiv.all_spouses
                      -- Present content sp: [sp]))
           in acc initially [] with acc ++ r) in
      if W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s151_b_applies_3
      then granted
      else granted ++ indiv.exempt_spouses))

  definition additional equals
    (output of AgedOrBlind with {
       -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- married: (output of St.FilingStatus with {
                      -- world: world -- injections: injections
                      -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                      -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).married
       -- surviving_spouse: (output of St.FilingStatus with {
                               -- world: world -- injections: injections
                               -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                               -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).surviving_spouse
       # `s63_f_1_B(Taxp,_,Taxy)` ends in `s151_b_applies(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy)`
       # with the spouse existentially quantified over the *whole* clause, so
       # the person §151(b) allows and the person over 65 are one and the same.
       # Cases inject the conclusion; a `tax/3` case derives it, and without
       # that half the standard deduction of a married couple over 65 is short
       # by one $600 entitlement. A grant that leaves its own spouse argument
       # free unifies with whichever spouse §7703 offers, so it admits them
       # all; one that names a spouse admits only that one. See D80.
       -- exempt_spouses: exempt_spouses
       }).additional

  exception definition additional
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3_3,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals
      (match (W.injected_money of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3_3,
                [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year], 2) with pattern
       -- Absent: $0
       -- Present content m: m)

  definition amount equals
    if not_eligible then $0 else basic + additional

  exception definition amount
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_c_1_3,
         [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
    consequence equals
      (match (W.injected_money of injections, P.pred_s63_c_1_3,
                [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1], 3) with pattern
       -- Absent: $0
       -- Present content m: m)

  exception definition amount
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3,
         [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
    consequence equals
      (match (W.injected_money of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3,
                [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1], 3) with pattern
       -- Absent: $0
       -- Present content m: m)
```

## (a), (b) and §63 itself — taxable income

(b) is for the individual who does not itemize, which the Prolog decides by
`\+ s63_d(Taxp,_,_,Taxy)` — no deduction events in the year at all. (a) is
everyone else: gross income less the §68-limited itemized total and the §151
personal exemptions. Both floor the result at zero.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope TaxableIncome:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output gross content money
  output itemizes content boolean
  output itemized_total content money
  ## after §68
  output deductions_allowed content money
  ## §151, both the total and the list of amounts (a) and (d)(2) need
  output exemptions content money
  output exemption_amounts content list of money
  ## s63_a/5 — the third argument
  output income_a content money
  ## s63_b/4 — the third argument
  output income_b content money
  ## s63/3
  output income content money
  ## §63 needs §151 to succeed. A *replaced* `s151/5` that names nobody
  ## relevant makes it fail rather than contribute zero -- see D39.
  output applies content boolean
```

```catala
scope TaxableIncome:
  ## §63(a) and (b) read `gross_income/3`, not `gross_income_individual/3`, so
  ## a taxpayer filing jointly is taxed on both incomes. §68 sees the same
  ## figure as its adjusted gross income, because this is what it is passed.
  definition gross equals
    (output of Inc.GrossIncome with {
       -- world: world -- person: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- joint_spouse:
            (output of S7703.JointFilingSpouse with {
               -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
               -- taxable_year: taxable_year
               -- qualifying_dependants:
                    (output of S152.QualifyingChildrenOf with {
                       -- injections: injections -- world: world
                       -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                       -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                       -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).children }).spouse
     }).total

  definition itemizes equals
    (output of ItemizedDeductions with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).itemizes

  ## A case may grant `s63_d/4` outright, which makes the taxpayer an itemizer
  ## even with no deduction events of their own.
  exception definition itemizes
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_d_4,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true

  definition itemized_total equals
    (output of ItemizedDeductions with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).total

  exception definition itemized_total
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s63_d_4,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals
      (match (W.injected_money of injections, P.pred_s63_d_4,
                [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year], 3) with pattern
       -- Absent: $0
       -- Present content m: m)

  definition deductions_allowed equals
    (output of S68.Section68 with {
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- status: S68.status_of_filing of
                    (output of St.FilingStatus with {
                       -- world: world -- injections: injections
                       -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).status
       -- agi: gross
       -- itemized_deductions: itemized_total }).deductions_out

  definition exemptions equals
    (output of S151.Personal with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).total

  definition exemption_amounts equals
    (output of S151.Personal with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).amounts

  # `s63(Taxp,Taxy,Taxinc) :- ( s63_b(...) ; ( \+ s63_b(...), s63_a(...) ) )`.
  # The standard-deduction branch needs §63(c); when a case *replaces* that
  # predicate (D22) and names nobody relevant, (b) fails, and with no itemized
  # deductions to fall back on §63 fails outright — so §1 does too and `tax/3`
  # reports zero. §63 itself can be replaced the same way.
  definition applies equals
    (W.pred_available of injections, P.pred_s63_3,
       [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
    and (itemizes
         or ((W.pred_available of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3,
                [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
             and (W.pred_available of injections, P.pred_s63_c_1_3,
                    [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
             and (W.pred_available of injections, P.pred_s63_c_2_3,
                    [taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1])
             and (W.pred_available of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3_3,
                    [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])))
    and (output of S151.Personal with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).applies

  definition income_a equals
    Money.max of $0, (gross - (deductions_allowed + exemptions))

  definition income_b equals
    Money.max of $0,
      (gross
       - (output of StandardDeduction with {
            -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
            -- taxable_year: taxable_year
            -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
            -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
            -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
            -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
            -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
            -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).amount
       - exemptions)

  ## §63 prefers (b) where it applies, and falls back to (a).
  definition income equals if itemizes then income_a else income_b
```

## Query surfaces for (a), (b), (c)(1) and (d)(2)

```catala-metadata
## s63_a(Taxp,Taxy,Taxinc,_,_) and s63_b(Taxp,Taxy,Taxinc,_)
declaration enumeration IncomeClause:
  -- SubsectionA
  -- SubsectionB

declaration scope TaxableIncomeHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input clause content IncomeClause
  input claimed content money
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output holds content boolean

## s63_c_1(Taxp,Taxy,Standed) and s63_c(Taxp,Taxy,Standed)
declaration scope StandardDeductionHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input claimed content money
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output holds content boolean

## s63_d_2(Taxp,Ded151,Taxy) -- `Ded151` is §151's *list* of exemption
## amounts, not the total.
declaration scope ExemptionListHolds:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input claimed content list of money
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  ## A grant of `s151/5` that leaves the list a Prolog variable unifies with
  ## whatever the case then claims.
  output granted_unconstrained content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope TaxableIncomeHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (let ti equals
       (output of TaxableIncome with {
          -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- taxable_year: taxable_year
          -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
          -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
          -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
          -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
          -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
          -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }) in
     match clause with pattern
     # (a) needs §63(d) to succeed, i.e. the taxpayer itemizes
     -- SubsectionA: ti.itemizes and ti.income_a = claimed
     # (b) needs it to fail
     -- SubsectionB: (not ti.itemizes) and ti.income_b = claimed)

scope StandardDeductionHolds:
  definition holds equals
    (output of StandardDeduction with {
       -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).amount = claimed

scope ExemptionListHolds:
  definition granted_unconstrained equals
    exists inj among
      (W.injections_for of injections, P.pred_s151_5,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    such that
      (match (List.nth_element of inj.args, 4) with pattern
       -- Absent: false
       -- Present content k: k = -1)

  definition holds equals
    granted_unconstrained
    or ((let ti equals
           (output of TaxableIncome with {
              -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
              -- taxable_year: taxable_year
              -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
              -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
              -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
              -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
              -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
              -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }) in
         # `s63_d_2(Taxp,Ded151,Taxy) :- s151(Taxp,_,_,Ded151,Taxy)`: with
         # `s151/5` replaced and no row for this taxpayer the call fails, and
         # an empty list of exemptions is not the same answer. See D39.
         ti.applies and ti.exemption_amounts = claimed))
```
